<script>
  import Meta from '../components/Meta.brm';
  import Icon from '../components/Icon.brm';
  import InstallCommand from '../components/InstallCommand.brm';
  import BenchChart from '../components/BenchChart.brm';
  import valuesTs from '../home/values-ts.md';
  import valuesNarra from '../home/values-narra.md';
  import effects from '../home/effects.md';
  import ToolDemo from '../components/ToolDemo.brm';
  import shapes from '../home/shapes.md';
  import { chapters } from '../pages.ts';
  import { $client } from 'brumate/signals';
  import { startTwoslash } from '../twoslash/client.ts';

  $client(() => {
    startTwoslash();
  }, 'idle');
</script>

<Meta
  title="Narra"
  description="Easy to read, hard to break. Narra is a compiled language built so you, your team and your tools can understand any piece of code at a glance."
  path=""
/>
<main class="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="hero-title">Narra</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Easy to read, hard to break. Narra is a compiled language built so you, your team and your tools can understand any piece of code at a glance.
      </p>
      <InstallCommand />
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/guide/01-getting-started">
          Start the guide
          <span class="button-icon"><Icon name="arrow-right" size=(16) /></span>
        </a>
        <a class="button quiet" href="/spec">Read the spec</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-code">
      <div class="window">
        <div class="window-bar">
          <span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
          <span class="window-title">shapes.nra</span>
        </div>
        {shapes.html}
      </div>
      <div class="rings" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400">
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="60" />
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="96" />
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="128" />
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="156" />
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="180" />
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="198" />
        </svg>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="speed">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-index">01</p>
      <h2 id="speed">Native binaries. Runs like <em>Rust.</em></h2>
      <p>Narra compiles to C, then to a native binary. On these benchmark programs it runs close to hand-written C and as fast as Go and Rust, and a hello world is 34 KB, the size of C's.</p>
    </header>
    <BenchChart />
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="values">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-index">02</p>
      <h2 id="values">Values never change <em>behind your back.</em></h2>
      <p>In TypeScript an object is shared: change it through one name and every name sees it. In Narra a value is a value. A change is written at the call with <code>mutable</code>, and a copy costs nothing until one side changes. No garbage collector, and no borrow checker to fight.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="compare">
      <figure class="compare-pane">
        <figcaption><span class="compare-lang">TypeScript</span><span class="compare-file">alias.ts</span></figcaption>
        {valuesTs.html}
        <div class="compare-output"><span class="compare-label">prints</span><code>70 <mark class="bad">70</mark></code><span class="compare-hint"><code>saved</code> changed too</span></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="compare-pane">
        <figcaption><span class="compare-lang">Narra</span><span class="compare-file">alias.nra</span></figcaption>
        {valuesNarra.html}
        <div class="compare-output"><span class="compare-label">prints</span><code>70 <mark class="good">100</mark></code><span class="compare-hint"><code>saved</code> kept its value</span></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="effects">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-index">03</p>
      <h2 id="effects">Read a signature, know <em>what it does.</em></h2>
      <p>An exported function lists what it does besides computing: <code>alloc</code> when it allocates memory, <code>io</code> when it touches files, the network or the terminal. You can tell which functions of a library are pure without reading their bodies. Inside a module the compiler works the effects out for you.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="effects">
      <figure class="window">
        <div class="window-bar">
          <span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
          <span class="window-title">shop.nra</span>
        </div>
        {effects.html}
      </figure>
      <ul class="effects-list">
        <li><code>total</code><span>pure: same input, same result, nothing else happens</span></li>
        <li><code>receipt</code><span><b>alloc</b>: builds a new string</span></li>
        <li><code>save</code><span><b>io</b>, <b>alloc</b>: writes a file</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="tools">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-index">04</p>
      <h2 id="tools">A compiler your <em>agent</em> can talk to.</h2>
      <p>Errors come as JSON with the edits that fix them, and the compiler answers questions about your code. A skill for Claude Code teaches the language: with it, an agent passed <a href="https://github.com/lxsmnsyc/narra/blob/main/skills/narra/evals/results.md">19 of 20 Narra tasks, against 15 of 20 without</a>.</p>
    </header>
    <ToolDemo />
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="learn">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-index">05</p>
      <h2 id="learn">Learn it one <em>small program</em> at a time.</h2>
      <p>Each chapter of the guide builds something that runs.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="chapters">
      #for (chapter, index of chapters by chapter.slug) {
        <li style=(`--item: ${index}`)>
          <a href=(`/guide/${chapter.slug}`)>
            <span class="chapter-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="chapter-title">{chapter.title.replace(/^\d+\.\s*/, '')}</span>
            <span class="chapter-arrow"><Icon name="arrow-right" size=(18) /></span>
          </a>
        </li>
      }
    </ol>
  </section>
</main>
